Subject: [PATCH] usb: generic: stop EHCI/OHCI at OS handoff

The generic host drivers allocate DMA memory but do not request removal
at OS handoff. EFI ExitBootServices() calls dm_remove_devices_active(),
which skips them without an active-DMA or OS-prepare flag.

On a Cubie A5E, OHCI HCCA was 0x7bf1f000 before EFI boot. Linux reused
that page for initramfs udevadm: its file offset 0x12080 mapped to physical
0x7bf1f080, exactly the old HCCA frame_no/pad1 writeback address. Three
bytes in an ELF relocation were overwritten by a frame counter. The
retained compressed initrd still matched its SHA256. Explicit usb stop
before the same EFI/GRUB boot prevented the corruption and allowed login.

Request normal driver removal at handoff, as explicit usb stop does,
rather than reserving leaked buffers or changing kernel/initrd data.
Cover the generic EHCI companion too so neither host retains active DMA.
This board-scoped patch is applied only when building A5E firmware.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/ehci-generic.c b/drivers/usb/host/ehci-generic.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/ehci-generic.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/ehci-generic.c
@@ -168,4 +168,4 @@
 	.ops	= &ehci_usb_ops,
 	.priv_auto	= sizeof(struct generic_ehci),
-	.flags	= DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA,
+	.flags	= DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA | DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE,
 };
diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/ohci-generic.c b/drivers/usb/host/ohci-generic.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/ohci-generic.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/ohci-generic.c
@@ -111,4 +111,4 @@
 	.ops	= &ohci_usb_ops,
 	.priv_auto	= sizeof(struct generic_ohci),
-	.flags	= DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA,
+	.flags	= DM_FLAG_ALLOC_PRIV_DMA | DM_FLAG_OS_PREPARE,
 };
